WEBVTT

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.460
The flow of time makes a continuous sound

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:32.260
Please come to the rooftop of the school's
south building after school on April 28th.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.260
Signed, Souma Sumire.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:33.930
It's a melody that invites the coming future
Signed, Souma Sumire.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.930
It's a melody that invites the coming future

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.060
Hey, Tomoki, there's a pretty
strange girl in your class, right?

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.810
A strange girl?
It's a melody that invites the coming future

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.680
Oh, yeah! You mean that weird chick with long hair.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.270
What kind of world is waiting for me?
Oh, yeah! You mean that weird chick with long hair.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.770
She's kinda like you.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:45.940
Like me?
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.610
She hardly ever talks and always
has this blank look on her face.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.360
It's like she's not interested in anyone around her.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.110
Her name's Haruki Misora.
What kind of world is waiting for me?

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.030
I tried asking myself for an answer
Her name's Haruki Misora.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.950
If you ask me, I'd say I'm pretty
talkative and expressive.
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.080
And my name is Asai Kei.
I tried asking myself for an answer

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.580
What's so similar about us?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.950
The atmosphere around you.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.040
It's like you both lack genuine feeling
whenever you do something.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.420
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.540
Is that how you see it?

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.210
Here, in the middle of ideals and reality

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.380
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.720
Hell, yeah!

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.970
So, what's this about Haruki?
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.140
Oh, she's not the one I wanted to ask you about.
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:20.720
The hands of the clock are being constantly moved

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.890
It's Souma Sumire.
You know, the one with short hair.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.470
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.230
Oh, that's the class rep of my class.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.400
I've talked to her a few times.
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.440
And earlier today, I found a letter in my shoe locker.
I'll do anything to erase all sadness

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.230
And earlier today, I found a letter in my shoe locker.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.480
It said she wants to meet me
on the rooftop tomorrow after school.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.820
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.280
She's totally gonna ask you out!
So, whatcha gonna do?

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.450
I'll check it out.
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.200
I have no reason to refuse her invitation.
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:41.660
Even if it means going back down the passage of dark stairs

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.580
There's something I want to protect no matter what

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.410
You see, that's a perfect example
of how you simply go with the flow!

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.960
There's something I want to protect no matter what

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:55.340
I'll say that out loud

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:03.680
Believing that fate will bring us together again

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.610
Hey, you're in Class 2-1, right?

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.450
Yes.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.870
Do you happen to know Souma?

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.200
Yes.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.280
Oh, great.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.450
She told me to meet her up here.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.160
Do you know where she might be?

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.330
No.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.340
Hey, what's your favorite food?

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.710
I don't have one.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.590
What's your least favorite food?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.840
I don't have one.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.260
Do you think we're alike?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.840
It depends on your definition of "alike."

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.020
By the way, why are you here?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.350
If you want to be left alone, I can just leave.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.940
I'm here because Souma Sumire
told me to come here.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.320
It's not that I want to be alone.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:59.490
I wish you'd said that when I brought Souma up.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.740
Do you talk to her often?

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:08.330
The classmate I talked to the most when
I was a first-year was Souma Sumire.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.290
Oh, so you <i>are</i> close.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:15.630
You're already becoming the person I've
talked to most since I became a second-year.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.360
Reset.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.470
That girl...

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.980
If you ask me, I'd say I'm pretty
talkative and expressive.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.240
And my name is Asai Kei.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.740
What's so similar about us?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.070
The atmosphere around you.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.160
It's like you both lack genuine feeling
whenever you do something.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.120
Yeah, we do.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.540
Hell, yeah!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.050
So, what's this about Haruki?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.880
Uh... Is something wrong?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.760
Oh, it's nothing. I was just thinking
I didn't have much of a chance.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:53.480
This place is called Sakurada.
It's a town tucked away in Japan,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:57.190
where about half of the people
possess special abilities.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.770
There are a vast range of abilities.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.030
While they generally defy the laws of physics,
they are pretty much useless for the most part.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.740
There's a reason why people
with abilities live in Sakurada:

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.700
If someone leaves Sakurada,
they end up forgetting about their ability.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:18.500
Being unaware of an ability you can use
is no different from not having one at all.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:24.630
I possess the ability to relive the past
in my mind with all five senses.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:30.220
I can always remember the things I've seen,
heard, and thought with absolute accuracy.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.560
So far, my ability has only been effective enough
to say that I've got a better memory than others.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.400
However...

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.690
Hey, where should we go?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.070
The place we went to last time!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.150
Sounds good. Let's go!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:44.990
Yeah, let's!
Sounds good. Let's go!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.790
Good afternoon, Asai.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.040
What are you doing, Souma?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.300
Doing my class rep duties.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.050
In a place like this?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.420
It doesn't matter where I do them.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.050
As long as it isn't on the rooftop
of the south building.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.720
Don't you think it's a bit rude when you ask me
to come somewhere and then not show up at all?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.970
My bad.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.390
Is it part of the class rep's duties
to set me and Haruki up?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.150
She doesn't have any friends she's close with.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.530
I just simply thought that if I have
you two meet, you'd become friends.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.990
And what about you?

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.610
I'll try, but I don't think it's possible.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.200
We're not compatible at all.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.290
Like you wouldn't believe.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.790
Why me, of all people?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.420
Because you're compatible.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.750
You two are really alike.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.960
You're identical in how you
both lead very proper lives.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.420
Not in that we both lack genuine feeling?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:53.050
If you ever wanna get closer to Haruki,
I don't mind helping you out.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.640
Is there any real point to that?

00:06:55.640 --> 00:07:00.390
There is. There's a huge meaning
to you two being together.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.400
Like, say for example, resetting.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.280
Reset.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.540
Oh, so this is the second time.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.120
Is resetting your ability?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.130
Yes.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.420
I can restore the world to as far as three days back.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.300
So you can basically rewind time?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.130
No. I just rearrange everything to its past state.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.890
Since I rearrange things,
I strictly reconstruct the world of the past.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.810
So it's not as if you're erasing time.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.390
It's really just a reset.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:45.440
Even human brain cells get
rearranged to their past state.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.650
Because of that, people lose
their memories of that time.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.070
I see.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.360
However, my ability has three restrictions to it.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:58.410
First of all, I can't use my ability
to reset if I didn't save beforehand.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.660
The save expires after 72 hours.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:07.920
Secondly, I can't save until 24 hours
have passed since a reset.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.630
So basically, you can't repeat
the same time over and over again.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:15.510
And lastly, the biggest restriction out of the three:

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.140
resetting personally affects me, too.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.430
All my memories of that time also disappear.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.520
Even the memory of the reset itself disappears.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.400
Spring is almost over.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.530
Summer starts next weekend.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:36.370
Oh, really? Summer is always
much sooner than you think.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:41.620
Well then, let's spend our summer here.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.370
We can meet up as much as we want

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:48.130
and talk about all sorts of things that can
help us understand each other better.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.500
Is there any point in doing that?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.510
Who cares if there's a point or not?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:59.010
We'll just be hanging out like sparrows that
are only on a power line to rest their wings.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.350
I don't like doing things without any purpose.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.350
I guess.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.980
Then, let's assume there's an android among us.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.440
An android?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.110
They look just like humans.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.320
Even if you were to hold their hand,
kiss them, or check their blood,

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.240
you wouldn't know that they're artificial.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.370
So, who among us is that kind of android?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.000
What's the point of this?

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.250
It's just a simple question.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.960
Who's an android?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.000
We're all just ordinary humans.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.470
Just think about it.
Who would you expect to be an android?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.340
Anyway, let's make figuring
that out a reason to meet up.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.720
And then, at the end of summer,
we'll tell each other our answers.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.850
Resetting, huh?

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.850
It's an interesting ability, but it's not very useful.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.400
Yeah, that's true.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.070
You simply experience the same time period twice.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.240
On top of that, you're not aware
that it's the second time.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.400
Normally.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.030
Huh?

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.990
It seems like resetting doesn't affect my memory.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.620
I think my special ability preserves it.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.250
Seriously?

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:10.880
Until now, I sometimes had this feeling as if
my memory and sense of time were doubled.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.090
I think it might have something
to do with Haruki's reset ability.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.930
You should totally reset after memorizing
the winning lottery ticket numbers!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.930
I'll do that when I'm completely
desperate for money.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.470
Totally saw that coming!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.310
You always take the high road.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:28.850
But I'm sure it can be used for good.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:29.940
Yeah.

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.940
It might break the rules of this world, after all.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:37.990
Reset.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.450
Oh, I don't have a save.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:44.910
Um...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.250
Do you happen to know my mom?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.120
No, I don't.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.750
Where did you lose sight of her?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:58.300
Please tell me what you've been doing up until now.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.550
I was at the hospital for a checkup.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.970
Please tell me your name.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.680
Kurakawa Mari.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:09.980
Please let go.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.130
Let's work together.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.210
Together?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.890
I won't lose my memory even
if you use your reset ability.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:46.010
So if we team up, we can redo the past.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.430
We can overcome any problem together.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.100
I don't want to.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.190
Why not?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.940
Because I abide by the rules.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:53.850
Rules?

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.860
It's a guideline for me to decide on things.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:57.860
For instance,

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:02.700
if it has a probability of causing a negative
effect on my surroundings, I refuse to reset.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:06.330
Will it cause a negative effect if we work together?

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.870
It's a possibility.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.040
How so?

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.580
Because you're the only one
who can exploit resetting.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.000
When I do a reset, I lose my memory of that time.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.460
I wouldn't even notice your lies.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.260
You have too much initiative in this situation.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.550
Plus, I don't have any basis to trust you.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.390
Haruki.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:32.810
You used your reset ability on this rooftop
after school on April 28th, right?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.940
Yes. Probably.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.110
I'm curious why you did it.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.980
It was probably because a girl was crying.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.360
Whenever I see someone crying, I reset.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.070
That's pointless.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.620
Even if you reset, she'll end up crying anyway.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.500
It being pointless isn't a reason
for breaking the rules.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.010
Haruki...

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:07.850
I'm sure I'll be able to earn your trust in due time.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:11.600
Not once have I ever trusted anyone.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:15.310
Is that so? Then, I'll be the first.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.150
Did you two warm up to each other?

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.860
I can't say. It's kinda difficult.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.450
Oh? So even you can admit when things are difficult.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.370
I started to wonder if she truly had anything to say.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:33.910
Kei, why do you want to get closer to Haruki?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.250
To get my hands on her reset ability.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:41.460
Kei, you're the kind of person that always gives
self-deprecating answers to such questions.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:45.090
It's caused by your extremely
strong sense of justice.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.510
I'd say it's on the same level
as clean-freaks or perfectionists.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.350
I don't think I'm that righteous.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:55.850
God once placed a curse on one young man.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.440
It was a curse that shot pain throughout the man's
entire body when he came across a sad person.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.900
Wow... That sounds terrible.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:08.160
In order to avoid his pain, the young man
reached out to all the sad people.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.410
And?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:13.660
God then made a copy of the
young man and created a fake.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:18.370
The copy had no will of its own,
so it did the same thing the original did.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:22.800
The fake also reached out to all the sad people.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:26.340
God gave the two names of their own, you know.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:27.760
What kind of names?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.260
He chose the names Good and Hypocrisy.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.970
So who do you think got which name?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.390
The real young man is Hypocrisy. The fake is Good.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.390
Why is that?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.520
The real one helps others for his own good.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.150
You don't even have to think
about who's genuinely good.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.860
The fake is only following the real one's lead.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.950
That isn't a problem.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.820
Doing things for yourself isn't genuinely good.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.490
That just shows how upright you are.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.330
Your sense of justice is so strong that
you can't even admit you're righteous.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.210
If there's even just a little bit of impurity within you,
you'll end up thinking like you're a villain.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.090
Haruki Misora is what you'd
consider to be an ideal human.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:11.220
She's the only being that can be what
you consider to be genuinely good.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.430
Let's find out about Haruki's past.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.720
We might find out how she
became the way that she is now.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.100
How?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.310
I know someone with the perfect ability for this.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.610
I think he'd probably be willing to help us out.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.610
What do you usually do to have fun?

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.610
I've been talking to this one person a lot lately.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.860
Today, we talked about trust.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:32.870
Trust?

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.620
It was about if it's possible
to accept a person's judgment

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.870
under circumstances when there's no logical basis.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.210
Okay...

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.210
He said he would earn my trust.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.710
So, that person likes you, huh?

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.880
Likes?

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.630
I like you. And I like my mom, too.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:56.640
But my mom doesn't like me. It's because I'm a fake.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.640
What do you mean by "fake"?

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.150
Do you want to be liked by your mother?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.400
Yeah. Very much.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.780
I'm here to pick you up, Mari.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.280
Let's go home.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.580
Who is this man?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.330
He's Mister Tsushima.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.160
Are you Haruki?

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:21.830
Yes.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.580
I heard about you from Mari.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.920
She said you always spend time with her.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.000
Thank you for that.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.880
Who are you?

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.550
I'm like her stand-in guardian.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:34.130
Why isn't Mari's mother coming to pick her up?

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:37.390
She will. She's just a little late, that's all.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.680
We need to get going, Mari.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.770
Okay.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:45.350
Where's Souma?

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.520
She's meeting someone, so she'll apparently be late.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.320
Your hair's really pretty.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:00.120
And since it's pretty, it might be best to cut it.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.250
I don't get what you mean.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.080
It doesn't feel real.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.710
Your pretty hair makes you
seem way too otherworldly.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.880
Is that a problem?

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:10.840
Maybe.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.880
Asai Kei, there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.220
What is it?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:19.720
Is it sad to be unloved by your mother?

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.520
Well, yeah, it would normally be sad.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.940
There's a girl named Kurakawa Mari.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.730
She wishes to be loved by her mother.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.690
Do you know of a way to make that happen?

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.610
You want to help her, right?

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:35.740
I don't really know.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:40.080
But I decided to be on her side.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.660
Following your own rules?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.450
No.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:43.500
Why, then?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.500
I'm not sure.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.710
If you want to help that girl out
no matter what, then I'll help out.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:54.840
But if you're helping the girl just for the sake of it,

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.130
then I don't want to.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:00.890
I can't do anything to force you.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.600
Kei! Haruki!

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.390
Let's go to the student council room.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:10.230
Nice to meet you. I'm the student
council president, Sakagami.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.690
His ability is a pretty interesting one.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.650
What? You haven't told them yet?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:15.400
Nope.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:21.070
B-Basically, my ability is copying the ability
of the person I'm touching with my right hand

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:24.120
to the person I'm touching with my left.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.290
I want you to copy Kei's ability of absolute memory to Haruki.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.040
We'll make you remember your childhood times.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:30.960
Why?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.630
Because I wanna know.
I'm really interested in your past.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.630
Is that so? All right, then.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.130
Hold on.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.890
Memories have tremendous power.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:44.060
It might distort your personality, Haruki.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.640
Is there a problem with that?

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.400
I understand. If there are any problems, let's reset.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:53.940
Save.

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:56.900
Go right ahead.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.780
Okay, here we go.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:04.330
If Asai uses his ability while we're like this,
Haruki will get the same effect.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.660
Haruki, what day do you want to remember?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.920
Well... Let's go back to when I was 5 years old.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.920
Got it. I'm starting now.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.150
What's wrong?

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.780
I was crying.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:40.490
Always.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:41.530
Always?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.280
I cried very often...

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:49.250
Whenever I heard sad news,
or even if something broke.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.920
Why did you cry?

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.790
Because it was sad.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.500
What was sad about it?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.880
Everything about it was sad.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.970
It's sad that everyone will die someday.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.300
It's sad that everything will break someday.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:08.270
Everything about those obvious rules is sad.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.770
The natural way of things is sad, huh?

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:11.850
Yes.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.600
That's why you became unable to choose.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.650
That's why you created rules.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:17.400
Yes.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.950
If anything and everything is tied to sadness,
then there's no point in having choices.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.160
No matter what you choose, it changes nothing.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.330
That's why you became unable to choose.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:31.960
You can't choose anything, and yet,
you must choose something.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.290
That is why you created rules for your own actions.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.130
Yes.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.340
I want you to tell me one thing, though.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.130
Who's the one who's sad?

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.180
I don't know.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:51.680
Haruki Misora, what you were
missing was your sense of self.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:57.190
The young Haruki didn't even realize
that what she was sad about was herself.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:01.190
If there wasn't any difference between
a death you saw on TV and your own,

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.950
then you wouldn't know how much
sadness there would be in the world.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:10.410
It must be very painful to live, feeling all the sadness
of the world as if it affects you personally.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:14.460
After getting your feelings worn down by sadness,
you become unable to do anything, right?

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:18.130
And yet, she still decided to keep going.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.250
She created rules to make the right decisions.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:24.220
She was forcing herself to try
and help even if she was unable to.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:28.600
And to always make the right choices,
even if it meant losing her emotions.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:33.980
I think only Haruki, who doesn't have
a sense of self, can remain righteous.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.980
If there really is a person out
there who we can call "Good,"

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:40.480
I'm sure it'd be Haruki.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.980
But Haruki isn't able to help anyone.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.200
People would rather get help, even from a hypocrite,

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.780
than to be watched over by a good person.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.240
I guess.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:55.620
Also, I think the ones who can save people
are selfish hypocrites like you, Kei.

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:59.130
There's no way. I'm not even a hypocrite.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:21:59.880
Right.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:02.920
You're kind to a fault,

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:05.920
and that uprightness of yours causes you
to worry too much about your own malice.

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:10.350
You're unable to believe that you're right,
yet you continue to be righteous.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.100
I don't get what you mean.

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:15.230
Let's prove it, then.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:16.390
Prove it?

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:20.310
I'll have you act as if you're a good person.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.820
I'm surprised. I wouldn't expect swings to suit you.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.700
Can you really say that about swings?

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:35.000
Probably. They definitely don't suit me.

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.250
You're Kurakawa Mari, right?

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:38.160
Yeah.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:44.250
Nice to meet you. I'm Asai.
I go to the same school as Haruki.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:46.130
I'd like to ask you something.

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:47.010
What?

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:53.510
Did you know that a little girl named
Kurakawa Mari died seven years ago?

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:56.850
Kurakawa Mari died seven years ago.

00:22:56.850 --> 00:22:57.890
She died?

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:02.480
When the doctor performed a C-section on Mari's
mother, Mari had already stopped breathing.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:09.450
Mari, if Kurakawa Mari died,
then who might you be?

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:29.510
You choose, Haruki.

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:30.760
Are you going to hand Mari over to the Bureau?

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:32.890
My job means doing things I don't want to do.

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:34.300
What do you want to do with Haruki Misora?

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:37.310
I remembered all of the sadness
I was supposed to feel soon.

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:37.680
Let's go erase the girl's tears.
I remembered all of the sadness
I was supposed to feel soon.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.940
Let's go erase the girl's tears.

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:48.570
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:56.080
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:56.660 --> 00:24:01.540
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:09.590
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:15.180
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:22.390
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:26.900
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:30.610
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:36.240
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:43.370
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:43.370 --> 00:24:50.000
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:57.050
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:57.050 --> 00:25:01.140
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:08.020
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
